# SECURITY-2D-3B — authoritative CI dependency INPUT (runtime + CI tooling).
#
# CI installs the SINGLE fully-resolved lock generated from THIS file
# (requirements-ci.lock) with one `pip install --require-hashes` call. That lock is a
# superset of requirements.lock: the exact same runtime graph plus the test/lint tools
# below, resolved together in one pass so the two locks can never disagree on a shared
# transitive version.
#
# Regenerate after editing (clean Linux / Python 3.13 environment — CI runs 3.13):
#     uv pip compile requirements-ci.in --generate-hashes \
#         --python-version 3.13 --python-platform linux -o requirements-ci.lock
#
# The production Docker image installs requirements.lock ONLY — it never receives these
# CI tools.

# Runtime intent (ranges + the alembic exact pin) comes from the runtime input verbatim.
-r requirements.in

# CI-only tooling. ruff is EXACT-pinned for the same reason alembic is: an unpinned bump
# reddened master on files no PR had touched (0.16.0 flagged 42 errors 0.15.22 did not).
ruff==0.15.22
pytest
pytest-cov
coverage
# psycopg2-binary: the real-PostgreSQL migration/EXPLAIN jobs connect over psycopg2.
# asyncpg is NOT repeated here — it is already a runtime dependency via requirements.in.
psycopg2-binary
